---
layout: null
sitemap: false
---
{%- comment -%}
  Search index for simple-jekyll-search. Reads only title / tags / description of existing posts,
  so no post needs to be edited. Fields: title, url, snippet (shown in results),
  tags, topic, series, type (searchable), keywords (accent-free, so "hermes birkin" finds "Hermès Birkin").
  The old "date" field was removed: simple-jekyll-search matches a query against EVERY field,
  so "jan" or "2027" matched all posts.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign tool_files = "sms-count.md,verify-email.md,qrcode.md,url-encode.md,html-encode.md,whatsapp.md,tiny.md,embeded-url.md,disc-test.md" | split: "," -%}
{%- assign first = true -%}
[
{%- for post in site.posts -%}
  {%- unless first -%},{%- endunless -%}
  {%- assign first = false -%}
  {%- assign tag_text = post.tags | join: " " -%}
  {%- assign kw = post.title | append: " " | append: tag_text | slugify: "latin" | replace: "-", " " %}
  {
    "title": {{ post.title | strip | jsonify }},
    "type": "guide",
    "tags": {{ post.tags | join: ", " | jsonify }},
    "topic": {{ post.topic | default: "" | jsonify }},
    "series": {{ post.series | default: "" | jsonify }},
    "keywords": {{ kw | jsonify }},
    "url": {{ post.url | absolute_url | jsonify }},
    "snippet": {{ post.description | default: post.excerpt | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | strip | truncate: 160 | jsonify }}
  }
{%- endfor -%}
{%- for p in site.pages -%}
  {%- if tool_files contains p.path -%}
    {%- unless first -%},{%- endunless -%}
    {%- assign first = false -%}
    {%- assign pkw = p.title | default: p.basename | append: " tool" | slugify: "latin" | replace: "-", " " %}
  {
    "title": {{ p.title | default: p.basename | strip | jsonify }},
    "type": "tool",
    "tags": "tool",
    "topic": "",
    "series": "",
    "keywords": {{ pkw | jsonify }},
    "url": {{ p.url | absolute_url | jsonify }},
    "snippet": {{ p.description | default: "" | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | strip | truncate: 160 | jsonify }}
  }
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor %}
]